MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug and Echo felt like useful additions because they would extend my Alexa setup to lamp control and hands-free commands alongside my Fire TV devices.",
    "The memory card and router connect to my recording and connected-device needs, although I would check card compatibility and only consider a router replacement if my connections needed improvement."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Fire TV Stick duplicates capabilities I already have through my Fire TV Stick 4K and Fire TV television, so sharing the same device family does not give me a reason to choose it.",
    "Speaker wire, a USB hub, and a keyboard and mouse do not solve a current problem for me. The large desktop drive feels excessive for my present storage needs, and the Kindle does not connect to what I am currently doing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning several electronics seems to have been taken as interest in general electronic accessories, even when I have no clear use for them.",
    "My use of Amazon devices seems to have been stretched into interest in more Amazon products, without enough attention to whether they add a useful capability or repeat one I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases center on watching, recording, and monitoring video at home; an addition needs a concrete role in those activities to interest me.",
    "I distinguish useful additions from replacements and speculative upgrades: recording storage needs to fit my camera, and a router only becomes compelling if my current network has problems."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my connected-home interests but missed how much my choices depend on a current need, compatibility, and adding something my existing devices do not already provide."
}
